€” scored by rubric/tolerance and A/B'd against a generic \"review this\" baseline, which it must beat on must-find recall (`MASTER-PLAN.md:23, 51-55`).\n\n**The committed method & contract**\n- Protocol v2 is the SKILL.md spec: TRIAGE â†’ FRAME deep-structure â†’ TYPE-APPROPRIATE LENS â†’ CROSS-CUTTING DIAGNOSIS with forcing functions (D1 widen / D2 disconfirm / D3 events-vs-structure) â†’ OPERATOR-WRONG PASS â†’ THREE-CHANNEL REPORT (what's-going-on / what-matters / what's-wrong) â†’ SCOPE-HONEST EVIDENCE (`MASTER-PLAN.md:26-35`).\n- A concrete output schema is committed (artifact_type, depth, frame, what_matters[], load_bearing[], findings[], operator_wrong_pass, needs_verification[], what_would_change_my_conclusion, residual_uncertainty), with **field types to be locked in Stage 2** (`MASTER-PLAN.md:37-41`).\n\n**What the core is NOT (machine-checkable non-goals)**\n- NOT a rewriter (schema is analysis, not replacement); NOT the Shark Tank (must be able to emit **zero defects + a populated what-matters** â€” a \"sound\" verdict is valid); NOT researchPrime (no self-CORROBORATED).\n- Every finding has a non-empty `location_span`; reasoning precedes verdict; `load_bearing` is a ranked list â‰¥0 (**not pinned to 1**); a \"sound/pass\" verdict **requires** populated what-matters â€” no empty flattery (`MASTER-PLAN.md:43-49`).\n\n**Deferred / open**\n- Residual decisions pre-registered for **Stage 2**: hypothesis count N, nitpick cap, LIGHT/FULL depth thresholds, the canary pass-bar + run-count for significance, schema field types, and the operator-wrong-pass scoring rubric (`MASTER-PLAN.md:61-63`).\n- The deferred \"magic\" advisor work (the generative-AND-vetted method, skill-to-skill composition, measurable \"magic,\" scope boundary, build sequencing) is tracked as five open problems in the handoff â€” and per the handoff's later updates that advisor cycle was itself subsequently researched, planned, and Shark-converged to a Foreman-ready state under `crucible-advisor\\` (`NEXT-SESSION-HANDOFF.md:3-23, 49-77`).\n\n**Status / next step**\n- Per the handoff, the diagnose-core is **researched, adversarially converged, and build-ready**; the next concrete action is the **Foreman build** (`NEXT-SESSION-HANDOFF.md:23, 36-42`).\n\nNote: the prompt's anchor list truncated G4 mid-sentence (\"NEVERâ€¦\"); the full file reads \"**NEVER self-assigns CORROBORATED/OBSERVED; NOT a rewriter; NOT the Shark Tank**\" â€” included above for completeness."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7768,"cache_read_input_tokens":30854,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7768},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f646581-2e4f-48fd-9945-e1efb375e3ce","uuid":"dcad75be-d6eb-48cd-8c27-182dfc0befa4","request_id":"req_011CcFpJYxpP2DZ4afdfgHg5"}
